{
  "dom_id": "step-q331827",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that $L\\{{t}^{n}\\}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},$ find the Laplace transform $L\\{{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {t}^{4}\\}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$\n\nUsing the given result, we have\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{4}\\}=\\frac{4!}{{s}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the first shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {t}^{4}\\} & =\\frac{4!}{(s+3)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{(s+3)^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
